Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Load Stochastic Binary Input", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.973449437308692*^9, 3.973449440399143*^9}, {
  3.9858565745694933`*^9, 
  3.9858565807225513`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b8bbd795-3841-4732-85b9-\
098aac10122b"],

Cell["\<\
We use a signal generation algorithm I developed some years ago to generate \
an input that has a binary probability density and a specifically designed \
auto-correlation function that will be used to perturb the unknown system. \
Such stochastic binary inputs deliver the maximum power to a system for \
minimum range. 
This input has been generated by other software written in Julia and saved in \
a file which we now load: \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.973449446926558*^9, 3.9734496227552843`*^9}, {
  3.973454768182605*^9, 3.973454778066135*^9}, {3.985855864582411*^9, 
  3.9858562042234907`*^9}, {3.985856886269321*^9, 
