Cell["\<\
Note that it is important that the input, x, (i.e., Scope Channel 1) and the \
output, y, (i.e., Scope Channel 2) be with in \[PlusMinus]2.56 V. The reason \
is that when voltages are higher than this then the Digilent Discovery 3 \
switches the ADC input ranges to \[PlusMinus]25 V which results in 10 x \
larger minimum values.
If we assume that the ADC is using its \[PlusMinus]2.56 V range, and we \
assume that because we are sampling at <50 MHz then we should be getting 16 \
bit conversions. Under these assumptions out minimum resolution in \[Mu]V \
should be:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9699888576588783`*^9, 3.969988989843717*^9}, {
  3.9734540772877827`*^9, 3.973454191873241*^9}, {3.973454418227689*^9, 
  3.97345442332266*^9}, {3.973515277723439*^9, 3.973515286120819*^9}, {
  3.984488815735064*^9, 
  3.984488820344277*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"429de212-803c-4fdc-8ecb-\
1846970f5f5c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  SuperscriptBox["10", "6"], 
  FractionBox["2.56", 
   SuperscriptBox["2", "15"]]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.973453572129318*^9, 3.9734536262467737`*^9}, {
   3.973454048202756*^9, 3.9734540616258574`*^9}, {3.9734542009521914`*^9, 
   3.973454201534172*^9}, {3.9734544011861143`*^9, 3.97345441381927*^9}, 
