Cell["\<\
The area under the system impulse response function should equal the system \
static gain. We can integrate the impulse response function to find the area \
under it. If the impulse response function was in the form of an equation \
then we could symbolically integrate it. However our estimate of the impulse \
response function is in non-parametric form (i.e., a list of numbers).  \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.970139341314474*^9, 3.970139634229245*^9}, 
   3.970146776467739*^9, {3.970149800706563*^9, 3.970149824032827*^9}, {
   3.970149920679737*^9, 3.97014994982491*^9}, {3.970150391150045*^9, 
   3.970150400812216*^9}, 3.970153464872373*^9, 
   3.970221284336177*^9},ExpressionUUID->"ab160df2-02ea-402b-ace6-\
2a0c5f09792f"],

Cell["\<\
A crude way to do numerical integration is rectangular integration:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.970221291146913*^9, 
  3.970221349032873*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"40292949-6e5c-4cc5-8dbf-\
ea03cc41eb57"],

