Cell["\<\
The prediction is so good it is difficult to distinguish the predicted output \
from the measured output.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.970151011702894*^9, 
  3.97015104642819*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cb130c83-e512-4f67-865c-\
c503e3de64d4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Determine the residuals between measured output and predicted output from the \
non-parametric model\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7812997077363963`*^9, 3.781299728412301*^9}, {
  3.781351611473714*^9, 3.7813516225179777`*^9}, {3.781351663211157*^9, 
  3.7813516637738934`*^9}, {3.781442265784892*^9, 3.781442272939454*^9}, {
  3.7814455972550435`*^9, 3.7814455981908364`*^9}, {3.8987682969873405`*^9, 
  3.898768298252473*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0a16cd15-dab7-402f-830a-\
d9499b83dd64"],

Cell["\<\
We can subtract the predicted output from the measured output to give the \
residuals (i.e., the output behavior that was not predicted). The residuals \
will be a combination of noise, higher-order dynamic behavior and \
nonlinearities. We will have to perform a nonlinear analysis to separate \
nonlinear behavior from measurement or system noise.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.781350215244328*^9, 3.7813503449548883`*^9}, {
  3.781351697557727*^9, 
  3.7813517115353966`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e10dfbc0-727c-4a31-9038-\
9dee7b66a3c2"],

