Cell["\<\
There is always a start up transient caused by the implicit assumption in \
convolution that the value of the input for t<0 is = 0. This causes an \
initial condition transient which often results in poor prediction for a \
length of the output equal to the time taken for the impulse response \
function to die down to zero. Lets look at this initial part of the predicted \
output: \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.970151222336335*^9, 
  3.970151453300741*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"24e9a48d-f2e4-4680-8d6e-\
9fd9128ad649"],

