Cell["\<\
We can see that the prediction error gets less as we increase time. If you \
look back at the estimated impulse response function you can see that it has \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]died down\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] to zero in about 3 \
ms. This is exactly how long it takes for the transient poor predictions to \
decay to near zero. For this reason is is common to trim off this initial \
artifact from any subsequent analyses. The number of samples we want to trim \
is:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97015155089287*^9, 3.970151687439864*^9}, {
  3.9701517336577663`*^9, 3.970151860726102*^9}, {3.970151906177734*^9, 
  3.970151932176606*^9}, {3.9704142556791286`*^9, 3.970414256191568*^9}, {
  3.984418591382456*^9, 3.984418591471655*^9}, {3.9845037745210543`*^9, 
  3.9845037746541367`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"13aec73b-d96d-4e75-890f-\
c4bb37615431"],

