Cell["\<\
The prediction is almost perfect. The low-pass nature of the system is clear \
(the high frequencies in the input do not appear in the output).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8983420504685044`*^9, 3.8983421231994486`*^9}, {
  3.898888563825178*^9, 3.8988885754995327`*^9}, {3.8988887112192855`*^9, 
  3.8988887118621187`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d83a3f89-06ea-4a6e-ae3d-\
3bc0f25f5b88"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["% Variance Accounted For (%VAF)", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.899031449556143*^9, 
  3.899031464472307*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f213226b-8a5c-4f58-872f-\
2c9c4ae80221"],

Cell["\<\
It is useful to have a single measure of the degree to which our model \
(parametric or non-parametric) can predict the output for a given input. One \
such measure is the variance accounted for. It tells use the % of the output \
variation (variance) which is accounted for by the model. If every nuance in \
the output is predicted by a model than the %VAF = 100%. Conversely, if none \
of the output is predicted by the model the %VAF = 0. As a general rule we \
normally want to see the %VAF well above 75%. For example, if the %VAF = 80% \
the the 20% unaccounted for by the model is some combination of noise and \
nonlinearity (you can only find out how much is noise vs nonlinearity by \
doing a nonlinear analysis (e.g., nonlinear system ID). Here we compute the \
%VAF after trimming off the initial transient:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8990314716731377`*^9, 3.899031874943247*^9}, {
  3.970152048891539*^9, 
  3.970152079761376*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"63f0b90e-818a-4113-a4db-\
eb1ac3fe4ee9"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  ButtonBox["\<\"\[GraySquare]\"\>",
   Appearance->"Frameless",
   ButtonFunction:>(SelectionMove[
      EvaluationCell[], All, TextLine]; SelectionEvaluate[
      EvaluationNotebook[]]),
   Evaluator->Automatic,
   Method->"Preemptive"], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"vafNP", "=", 
   RowBox[{"100", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", "-", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"Variance", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"ynp", "-", "y2"}], ")"}], "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"nTrim", ";;", "All"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
       RowBox[{"Variance", "[", 
        RowBox[{"y2", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"nTrim", ";;", "All"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]]}], 
     ")"}]}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969546329383287*^9, 3.9695464247211313`*^9}, {
   3.9695465545212927`*^9, 3.969546617567232*^9}, {3.969546669275358*^9, 
   3.969546691715456*^9}, {3.969546769236844*^9, 3.969546780409545*^9}, {
   3.970152018514737*^9, 3.970152028176587*^9}, 3.970153592269643*^9, {
   3.970163179716836*^9, 3.97016318048112*^9}, 3.9701633270055532`*^9, {
   3.970414269105487*^9, 3.9704142722315483`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
