Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Coherence Squared Function", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8989567496534586`*^9, 3.8989567529654546`*^9}, {
  3.898957058880369*^9, 
  3.898957060341535*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6599147f-f5e9-4110-a8e6-\
f406710ab934"],

Cell["\<\
The non-parametric frequency response function (like its inverse Fourier \
transform, the non-parametric system impulse response function) is the best \
linear dynamic model between the input and the output (remember that at this \
point we have not restricted the model order in any way). We would like to \
know how well the frequency response model predicts the output as a function \
of frequency. The coherence squared function, frCohSq, does exactly this. \
Indeed just as the percentage variance accounted for (%VAF) gives the overall \
% with which the output variation is predicted by the input, the % coherence \
squared  function gives the % variance accounted for at each frequency.  

Coherence squared values of less that 50% are considered to be low in \
engineering and physics.

There are two ways in which the % coherence squared may be low: 
1. is because of nonlinearities (often systems may be found to be linear over \
a range of input frequencies but then behave nonlinearly outside this range); 
2. is because at certain frequencies the additive \
(\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]measurement\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]) noise to the \
output may be higher at some frequencies than others.
It is not possible to tell just by looking a the coherence squared function \
whether low coherence squared values are due to noise or nonlinearities.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.898956762445453*^9, 3.8989573406795435`*^9}, {
  3.8990305132808957`*^9, 3.8990305708618755`*^9}, {3.970152738917996*^9, 
  3.970152744573703*^9}, {3.970414652937118*^9, 3.970414787564636*^9}, {
  3.970414831248329*^9, 
  3.9704148331919117`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"03316175-507c-4fba-bfba-\
2fabb88e8b38"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  ButtonBox["\<\"\[GraySquare]\"\>",
   Appearance->"Frameless",
   ButtonFunction:>(SelectionMove[
      EvaluationCell[], All, TextLine]; SelectionEvaluate[
      EvaluationNotebook[]]),
   Evaluator->Automatic,
   Method->"Preemptive"], ";", 
  RowBox[{"frCohSq", "=", 
   FractionBox[
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{"xyps", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{"All", ",", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "2"], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"xps", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{"All", ",", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"yps", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{"All", ",", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]]}], ";"}]], "Input",
