Cell["\<\
It can be seen that the cut-off frequency (natural frequency), \[Omega], is \
very close to 1 kHz (or 2\[Pi] 1000 rad/s).

A simple low-pass, second-order system is defined by three parameters: the \
static gain, \[Alpha], the natural frequency, \[Omega], and the damping \
parameter, \[Zeta].  As yet we have not estimated the value of the damping \
parameter but from experience it looks as though it is somewhere less than \
0.5 but greater than 0.1.

In the following we allow all three parameters to be adjusted to give a feel \
for the effect each has on the features of the Bode plot. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7958853971895037`*^9, 3.795885428288305*^9}, {
   3.795885482139207*^9, 3.7958857563093452`*^9}, 3.910713952498667*^9, 
   3.9191862991835537`*^9, 3.96954366232465*^9, {3.970156302616249*^9, 
   3.970156310895525*^9}, {3.970221630755458*^9, 
   3.970221658998163*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"03f9ef5f-2b3f-4bfe-a55a-\
57259f806553"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Fit a Parametric Second-Order Transfer Function Model by Hand\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.795798077887012*^9, 3.7957981026325855`*^9}, {
  3.7958098779886637`*^9, 
  3.795809880269731*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e534414e-8bb6-47ed-9b68-\
d96829e34aa9"],

Cell["\<\
As shown before the general equation for the transfer function of a \
second-order low-pass filter is:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.795798108024832*^9, 3.7957981519245596`*^9}, {
  3.970159374056982*^9, 
  3.970159381496187*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0b043d7e-66b5-4754-886b-\
a43555e2e193"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  ButtonBox["\<\"\[GraySquare]\"\>",
   Appearance->"Frameless",
   ButtonFunction:>(SelectionMove[
      EvaluationCell[], All, TextLine]; SelectionEvaluate[
      EvaluationNotebook[]]),
   Evaluator->Automatic,
   Method->"Preemptive"], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"H", "[", 
    RowBox[{"s_", ",", "\[Alpha]_", ",", "\[Omega]_", ",", "\[Zeta]_"}], 
    "]"}], ":=", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"]}], 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["s", "2"], "+", 
     RowBox[{"2", "\[Zeta]", " ", "\[Omega]", " ", "s"}], "+", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"]}]]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.795798156957447*^9, 3.7957982612023764`*^9}, 
   3.795811951276453*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[223]:=",ExpressionUUID->"e3723cc6-0cf3-4bf2-b903-b3970566338a"],

Cell["\<\
where the static gain is \[Alpha], the natural frequency (in radians/s) is \
\[Omega], and the damping parameter is \[Zeta].\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.795807739015408*^9, 
  3.795807789760621*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1c298955-2eb3-4dda-b350-\
1c4ef89ea4cd"],

Cell["\<\
Lets fit the transfer function by hand. Remember that the coherence squared \
function values are low at higher frequencies so you should be more careful \
in fitting low frequency values than those at high frequencies:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.795798279738632*^9, 3.7957982942889915`*^9}, {
  3.9701567490873423`*^9, 
  3.970156832980386*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"daf969d4-9b6f-4b14-a9f9-\
63bf25c215eb"],

