Cell["\<\
We can see that we could set \[Omega] = 1 kHz without much loss of fit.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9711184149809723`*^9, 3.971118446329364*^9}, {
  3.9711203323645144`*^9, 
  3.97112034625126*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5a515b03-7abc-47dc-8f85-\
ed4c50cfb89a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Sallen -Key Filter", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.794933814114971*^9, 
  3.794933822747094*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e4d51c3f-ccb6-4bca-a3ff-\
581681d746eb"],

Cell["\<\
We now open up the Black Box: It actually consists of a Sallen-Key filter \
which has been carefully designed to have a static gain \[Alpha] = 2, a \
natural frequency of \[Omega] = 2\[Pi] 1000 Hz and a damping parameter, \
\[Zeta] = 0.3.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.795810852108714*^9, 3.795810914141137*^9}, {
  3.970164026304185*^9, 3.970164158103259*^9}, {3.970768096241932*^9, 
  3.970768100363402*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ed347acf-eac6-4525-b3c8-\
9673892551ec"],

Cell["\<\
In previous notes we used the following second-order Sallen-Key filter has \
the following circuit:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.795810921894399*^9, 3.7958109591993504`*^9}, {
  3.970164161583548*^9, 
  3.9701641828508244`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8d8b388e-1293-4d96-ad58-\
